 2. 💰 Gravy for GDP 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Bureau of Economic Analysis. Chart: Courtenay Brown/Axios The U.S. economy grew substantially faster this summer than initially thought, Axios' Courtenay Brown writes .

 The economy is on remarkably strong footing heading into year-end, though inflation remains stubbornly high. By the numbers: The economy expanded at a 4.3% annualized rate, up from the 3.4% initially reported.

